CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
SUCCESSFUL
--
The SV-COMP tool-info module reads TRUE when any output line contains
SUCCESSFUL, so a run that finds a violation must not print the word
anywhere, not even in a status message.
